# The keeper a landscape has (docs/VISION.md §3), walked to and fought with real
# keys: the Coast's reaper on the ground it holds, found by where it dens.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/sentinels.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=axe_felling
#
# What it proves, in order: a keeper stands where it dens and holds the
# ground round it; a blow into its plated side rings off; it tells before it bites
# and the tell hangs over the side that is about to take you; dodging the bite
# leaves its working part open and a blow there hurts it; the side to be on MOVES
# as it comes apart, and nothing says so but the body; and the slate reads it off
# the same simulation while the key is held.
#
# What is NOT here, and why: its death, and the other two ways it can be taken.
# Killing it is five or six more of the same pass, and a scripted player fed to a
# boss for two minutes is downed about as often as it lands a blow — which makes a
# tour that measures the runner and not the game. Its death, its phases, the
# openings it gives and what its fall changes are proved in the real simulation,
# headless and without luck, in tests/sentinel/test_fight.gd; the tide flats and
# its works are rules, and are proved in tests/sentinel/test_ways.gd. Neither
# could be staged honestly on this seed anyway: no patch of tide flat wide enough
# to stand on lies inside the ground it holds.

# Stood by the keeper itself, never by the nearest intake: a keeper dens at the
# station it can feed from and at none within CLEAR_OF_HOME of the spawn, so
# `place intake` can name one it is not at (seed 1's only intake is 28 tiles
# from the spawn, and its reaper dens 189 tiles off). Seed 7's reaper dens at an
# intake with room all round it for the pass below.
coast calm
near keeper
wait 0.6
await sentinel 12
shot 01-the-keeper-at-its-intake with mob:sentinel.coast,prop:intake,land:coast

# Its ground: everything inside its reach is held while it stands.
walkto mob 8
await sentinel_reach 6
shot 02-inside-the-keepers-guard with mob:sentinel.coast,sentinel_reach

# The plated side: a blow anywhere but the working part rings off it.
try 4
  walkto plate 6
  tap swing
  await ring 4
end
shot 03-a-blow-off-its-plate with mob:sentinel.coast

# It tells before it bites, and the tell stands over the drum: the thing about to
# take you is the thing you have to hit.
try 4
  walkto mob 6
  await tell 14
end
shot 04-the-tell-over-its-drum with mob:sentinel.coast

# The pass a player learns: in front of it where it will bite, out of the bite as
# the tell starts, and into the drum while it is jammed and grinding round. Its
# working side in this phase is its FRONT, so there is nowhere safe to stand and
# swing: the dodge is the whole of the opening.
try 8
  walkto mob 6
  await tell 14
  press dodge 0.12
  await sentinel_open 6
  walkto part 2
  tap swing
  await hit 5
end
shot 05-into-the-working-part with mob:sentinel.coast,sentinel_hurt

# The side to be on MOVES as it comes apart. Nothing is said about it: the arch
# rears, the drum comes up out of the row, and what is open now is the drive in
# its left leg. Each pass is a player's: wait for the opening, take it, get out.
try 10
  walkto mob 6
  await tell 14
  press dodge 0.12
  walkto part 2
  tap swing
  await hit 5
  await sentinel_phase:raised 1
end
shot 06-the-arch-rears-and-its-side-moves with mob:sentinel.coast,sentinel_phase:raised

# And what the slate makes of it, held under the key: a keeper reads like any
# other machine, off the same simulation — its powers, the side that is open NOW,
# and what it is thinking. The phase it is in is what the read says, because the
# phase IS the row (src/core/sentinel/sentinel_phase.gd).
hold target
await target 6
shot 07-the-keeper-read-under-the-key with mob:sentinel.coast,target
release target

# Taking it down from here is the same pass again and again, and it is proved
# where a real-time tour cannot prove it honestly: tests/sentinel/test_fight.gd
# fights both keepers to death in the real simulation, through the openings they
# give, and holds what their fall changes.
